  "editorial": {
    "status": "working-edition",
    "notes": "The Angelus outside Paschaltide, with all three Hail Marys expanded. Its V. lines are assigned to a leader, not to a priest: the prayer is commonly said in groups and requires no clerical minister. No speaker is assigned to the Hail Marys: devotional practice may say each one together or divide it at Sancta Maria, and the edition does not prescribe either custom. The following Gloria Patri found in some prayer-book presentations is a separate prayer and is not appended here.",
